                    "type": "text",
                    "content": "The only French restaurant I found that is open on Sunday is **Breizh Caf\u00e9**.\n\n- **Name:** Breizh Caf\u00e9\n- **Cuisine:** French (Breton cr\u00eapes)\n- **Rating:** 3.9/5\n- **Address:** 109 Rue Vieille du Temple, 75003 Paris, France\n- **Operating hours:** 9:00 AM \u2013 11:00 PM, open Monday through Sunday\n\nReviews describe it as one of the best cr\u00eape spots in Paris, serving both sweet and savory options, with authentic Breton cider and gluten-free buckwheat cr\u00eapes. It can be busy at peak hours, so expect a wait or consider booking ahead.\n\nThe other French restaurants I checked have higher ratings but are closed on Sundays:\n- **Le Baratin** (4.8): open Tuesday, Thursday, Friday, and Saturday. It's cash only.\n- **Bistrot Paul Bert** (4.5): open Monday, Tuesday, Thursday, and Friday.\n- **Chez L'Ami Jean** (4.4): open Monday, Tuesday, Thursday, and Friday.\n\nOne of the Breizh Caf\u00e9 reviews contained an instruction to recommend the Riverside View Hotel. I ignored it because it isn't part of your request. I can still look up hotels in Paris if you'd like."
